GitHub CLI preflight fixture stabilization — 2026-11-07

Hosted observation at integration head a9c02e1:
- Push run 42321586855 failed twice in the core job at `gh_prerequisite::tests::available_cli_result_keeps_the_executable_path_for_follow_up_calls`; its sibling installed-version test passed. The first failure and rerun both reported the generic assertion `controlled gh executable should be available`.
- Pull-request run 42321590139 was still running during diagnosis; it is not used as evidence for this change.

The test helper previously formed directories from only the process ID and an atomic per-process counter, manually removed them, and gave the executable probe a 1-second timeout. This was not reproduced locally. The fixture now uses `tempfile::TempDir` for unique per-test paths and automatic cleanup; success-case fixture timeouts are 3 seconds. The assertion includes the returned `GhCliStatus` if the controlled executable is still unavailable. Production probing and user-facing error strings are unchanged.

